    {
      "title": "PM Modi launches development projects worth ₹14,000 crore in Gujarat",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/pm-modi-launches-development-projects-worth-14-000-crore-in-gujarat-126103000653_1.html",
      "description": "Prime Minister Narendra Modi said on Friday that he would serve the people of India till his last breath, an assertion coming days after Congress president Mallikarjun Kharge's remark, \"Modi ka baap bhi jayega\".\nHe was addressing a gathering after inaugurating the Bharat Bovine Breeding and Research Centre at Bhildi in Gujarat's Banaskantha district, launching and laying the foundation stone for development projects worth Rs 14,000 crore.\n\"Jeevan ke antim kshan tak janta ki seva main hi juta rahunga (I will continue to serve the people until my last breath),\" Modi said.\nIn an apparent jab at the Opposition, he said there are some people who get happiness when the country faces difficulty.\n\"They spread rumours after the Iran war that farmers would not get fertilisers, and people would not get LPG, as they wanted to defame Modi,\" the PM said.\nModi said his government has always prioritised the welfare of farmers and empowered them.\n\"Amid global uncertainties, fertiliser prices saw",
